  "description": "VESWEX crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P 1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C203 H259 Gd8 N7 O39,C3 H7 N1 O1. From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Gd5 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd6 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd7 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd8 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd9? (Gd) has 0 O neighbors; Gd10? (Gd) has 0 O neighbors; Gd11? (Gd) has 0 O neighbors; Gd12? (Gd) has 0 O neighbors; Gd13? (Gd) has 0 O neighbors; Gd14? (Gd) has 0 O neighbors; Gd15? (Gd) has 0 O neighbors; Gd16? (Gd) has 0 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 10 pairs, 9 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.611-4.881 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 91.11-170.17°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C203H259Gd8N7O39·C3H7NO.",
